  "programming": {
    "id": "numeral-triangles",
    "definition": {
      "title": "Numeral Triangles",
      "statement": "## Standard input and output\n\nEach run handles **one** case. Read from standard input and print the result to standard output. Do not read a case count or print case numbers, prompts, or labels. Use the line structure shown in the test-case input below.\n\n### Problem\n\nConstruct a Numeral Hex Triangle according to the following rules. You will be given three positive integers: s, a starting number; d, a delta (the amount by which to increase each number in the triangle); and r the number of rows. The numbers s and d will be in hexadecimal.\n\n1. The first row contains the number s.\n\n2. Each of the next rows has one more number than the previous row.\n\n3. Each number in the triangle is d more than the previous number in the triangle.\n\nHere are two examples of Numeral Hex Triangles:\n\nstart=A, delta=9, rows=5\n\n{{diagram:p-cccd71c112db69e7}}\n\nstart=ABC, delta=F, rows=4\n\n{{diagram:p-905fc5b1d353a25b}}\n\n### Input\n\nThe input has 3 positive integers, s, d, and r. The numbers are separated by spaces and each is less than $1{,}000{,}000_{16}$. Recall that $s$ and $d$ are in hexadecimal.\n\n### Output\n\nAdd all the hexadecimal digits in the numbers on row $r$. Reduce this sum to a single hexadecimal digit by repeatedly adding its hexadecimal digits until only one digit remains. Output that digit.\n\nFor example, if the last row contains $1A_{16}$, $1F_{16}$, and $24_{16}$, their digits sum to $1+A+1+F+2+4=21_{16}$. Since this has two hexadecimal digits, add them again: $2_{16}+1_{16}=3_{16}$. Output `3`.\n",
      "mode": "stdio",
      "comparator": "tokens",
      "timeLimitMs": 2000,
      "memoryLimitMb": 256,
      "starterCode": "# Read one case from standard input.\n# Print the result to standard output.\n",
      "samples": [
        {
          "input": "A 9 5\n",
          "expected": "5\n"
        },
        {
          "input": "ABC F 4\n",
          "expected": "C\n"
        },
        {
          "input": "BAD 50 10\n",
          "expected": "A\n"
        },
        {
          "input": "FED ABC 25\n",
          "expected": "F\n"
        },
        {
          "input": "184 231 35\n",
          "expected": "5\n"
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
